    "firstAnswerText": "Partial answer — points supported by the documentation:\n\nWeave's tracing is built on Ops, Calls, Traces, and Threads [S4]. [S4]\nFor agents, the Agents view gives a turn-by-turn record of conversations, with token usage, tool invocations, and execution spans [S2]. [S2]\nAn Evaluation object defines test examples (a dataset or list) and one or more scoring functions. You run it against a Model or custom function, and each .evaluate() call is an evaluation run [S3]. [S3]\nThe aim is to measure behavior on repeatable test cases, compare changes over time, and spot regressions [S3]. [S3]\n\nStill unresolved:\n\nExplain the role of tracing in Weave and how it relates to evaluations and Signals.\nExplain the role of evaluations in Weave and how they relate to tracing and Signals.\nExplain the role of Signals in Weave and how they relate to tracing and evaluations.",
    "finalAnswerText": "Partial answer — points supported by the documentation:\n\nWeave's tracing is built on Ops, Calls, Traces, and Threads [S4]. [S4]\nFor agents, the Agents view gives a turn-by-turn record of conversations, with token usage, tool invocations, and execution spans [S2]. [S2]\nAn Evaluation object defines test examples (a dataset or list) and one or more scoring functions. You run it against a Model or custom function, and each .evaluate() call is an evaluation run [S3]. [S3]\nThe aim is to measure behavior on repeatable test cases, compare changes over time, and spot regressions [S3]. [S3]\n\nStill unresolved:\n\nExplain the role of tracing in Weave and how it relates to evaluations and Signals.\nExplain the role of evaluations in Weave and how they relate to tracing and Signals.\nExplain the role of Signals in Weave and how they relate to tracing and evaluations.",
